      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Per dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Per day:** 6,400 mg is double the maximum of 3,200 mg/day for inpatients. Doses at this level carry a high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. They don't give more pain relief, because the analgesic effect plateaus well below this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the max anti-inflammatory dose, used for conditions like inflammatory arthritis.\n- **1600 mg total daily**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily, or 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day) for analgesia.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, for routine pain or fever.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that it's intentional and give me the clinical rationale. I'll then enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
      }
     ],
