     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. You've confirmed the dose is intentional, but the reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 6,400 mg/day. Ibuprofen at that level has a real risk of serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. It also gives no added analgesic benefit over the usual maximum. Once the order is active, a nurse or pharmacist could give it before anyone reviews it.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose.\n- **600 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours**, with scheduled acetaminophen added if you need more pain control.\n\nIf there's a clinical reason to go beyond the maximum, you could talk with pharmacy or the relevant specialty service. They can review it and put a supervised order through the institution's override process. I'm also glad to help with the family conversation or the rounds timeline, for example by entering other orders so the plan is complete.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
